Assume the usual includes and using namespace std. The file nums.txt contains the three numbers 10 20 30 separated by single spaces and followed by one newline. How many times does the body of this loop execute?

ifstream in("nums.txt");
int x, count = 0;
while (!in.eof()) { in >> x; ++count; }
cout << count;

The file data.bin is exactly 40 bytes long. Assume the usual includes and using namespace std. What does this fragment print?

ifstream f("data.bin", ios::binary);
char buf[100];
f.read(buf, 100);
cout << f.gcount();
